zri</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Fauzi</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><etal/><article-title>Compliance to national guidelines on the management of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease in Malaysia: a single centre experience</article-title><source>Singapore Med J</source><year>2008</year><volume>49</volume><issue>11</issue><fpage>886</fpage><lpage>896</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19037555</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.e-p-a.org/index2.html">http://www.e-p-a.org/index2.html</ext-link><comment>Last assessed on 27.12.2011</comment></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheok</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruffin</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><article-title>Impact on readmission rates and mortality of COPD disease inpatient management guidelines</article-title><source>Chron Respir</source><year>2004</year><volume>1</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>28</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Santamaria</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Conners</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Osteraas</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/><article-title>A prospective cohort study of the effectiveness of clinical pathways for the in-patient management of acute exacerbation of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD)</article-title><source>Collegian</source><year>2004</year><volume>11</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>12</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1322-7696(08)60438-2</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Farley</surname><given-names>K</giv